"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data, leveraging AI, IoT, and Web3. The project kicked off on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. Initial budget allocations included $500,000 for Phase One, which was later superseded by a total executive-approved budget of $2M covering research, development, and marketing. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing), and specialized training with a $15,000 budget has been approved. Key developments include a call for AI-driven data visualization ideas (due July 20th), a partnership exploration with TechInnovate, and a compliance plan budget increase to $55,000. Recent progress in Phase Two highlights a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is currently being sought, with a deadline at the end of November."
